    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paenultĭmus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pēn-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		paene-ultimus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the last but one</i> (post-class. for proximus a
			postremo, <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 64, 217</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paenultima meta November,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ecl. Quotae Cal. Sint Mens.
				12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pae-nultĭma</span></b> , ae, f.
			(sc. syllaba), <i>the penultimate syllable</i>, <i>the penult</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paenultimam circumflectere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					4, 7, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
